{"schema_version":3,"catalogue_version":1,"id":"bco:21-6","provision":"BCO 21-6","book":"bco","book_name":"Book of Church Order","abbreviation":"BCO","reference":"21-6","title":"Section 21-6","supplementary":false,"canonical_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/provisions/bco/21-6/","reader_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-constitution-reader/#bco/21-6","current_text":{"html":"<p>The candidate having answered these questions in the affirmative, the presiding minister shall propose to the church the following questions: <b>1. Do you, the people of this congregation, continue to profess your readiness to receive</b> _________________,<b> whom you have called to be your pastor?</b> <b>2. Do you promise to receive the word of truth from his mouth with meekness and love, and to submit to him in the due exercise of discipline?</b> <b>3. Do you promise to encourage him in his labors, and to assist his endeavors for your instruction and spiritual edification?</b> <b>4. Do you engage to continue to him while he is your pastor that competent worldly maintenance which you have promised, and to furnish him with whatever you may see needful for the honor of religion and for his comfort among you?</b></p>","text":"The candidate having answered these questions in the affirmative, the presiding minister shall propose to the church the following questions: 1. Do you, the people of this congregation, continue to profess your readiness to receive _________________, whom you have called to be your pastor? 2. Do you promise to receive the word of truth from his mouth with meekness and love, and to submit to him in the due exercise of discipline? 3. Do you promise to encourage him in his labors, and to assist his endeavors for your instruction and spiritual edification? 4. Do you engage to continue to him while he is your pastor that competent worldly maintenance which you have promised, and to furnish him with whatever you may see needful for the honor of religion and for his comfort among you?"},"source":{"name":"PCA Constitution Reader","revision":"14d73f7e5caf1d22e0514870dd30fcc69f8165cc","edition":"Current Reader text","files":{"bco.js":"c88e552545b73fd9690de620b237895b7ea52a94bed8e95690c116bf76be8ae5","wcf.js":"1ebf9e54223f7fe4e728a3e640c833a435af825d74b5ef3d4b04687685538a0d","wlc.js":"f6977e761ea4ccc93b07fcacfd0391890cb05b42f4317d807fa293c078d9b051","wsc.js":"dd775417f7ef21e3283bacad5e6ef193c41d64d03bd5a2e8fb934ccca8cb8e53","rao.js":"49808bbb0e95abdc3b07506c87dde0d62d087851e869b49c0f1f2424986450ec"}},"input_fingerprint":"38e35af46c8cbdb12a9a00c82d72f7192575b5ec27348534148f2a834551edc4","assessment_fingerprint":"517b100d2e9006e313ab6d84d4f0f31593b77832f395383ba2227779470cd034","assessment_summary":{"status":"stale","file":"index/provision_link_adjudications.jsonl","total":11481,"expected":12454,"applied":0,"stale":11481,"unmatched":0,"unassessed":12454},"parent_id":"bco:21","children":[],"coverage":{"relationships":"indexed_records","recommendations":{"status":"incomplete","note":"Recommendation and study papers are not comprehensively indexed by provision."},"history":"partial"},"relationship_count":25,"relationships":[{"id":"bco:21-6--ccb_advice:inquiries/ga33_2005__ci02.md","record_id":"ccb_advice:inquiries/ga33_2005__ci02.md","type":"CCB advice","title":"Relationship of Assistant Pastor to the Church","year":2005,"disposition":"in conflict","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga33_2005__ci02.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga33_2005__ci02.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:21-6--ccb_advice:inquiries/ga33_2005__ci02.md:occ-8a1ed4fce228","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga33_2005__ci02.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga33_2005__ci02.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["index/inquiries_search.json:provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga33_2005__ci02.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"summary":"An overture detailing how assistant pastors are called was found in conflict with BCO 3-2 and 12-2 through 12-4, as the relationship of an assistant pastor to a congregation is best left to the session."}},{"id":"bco:21-6--inquiry:inquiries/ga14_1986__ci16.md","record_id":"inquiry:inquiries/ga14_1986__ci16.md","type":"Constitutional inquiry","title":"Call of assistant pastor from another denomination without presbyterial examination","year":1986,"disposition":"advice given","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga14_1986__ci16.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga14_1986__ci16.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:21-6--inquiry:inquiries/ga14_1986__ci16.md:occ-6308c9ec48b4","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga14_1986__ci16.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga14_1986__ci16.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["index/inquiries_search.json:provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga14_1986__ci16.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"summary":"A session may not call an ordained assistant pastor from another denomination without presbytery approval and examination, as all teaching elders must be members of the serving presbytery."}},{"id":"bco:21-6--case:cases/ga52_2025__2024-05.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga52_2025__2024-05.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Bigelow v. North Florida Presbytery","year":2025,"disposition":"granted","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga52_2025__2024-05.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga52_2025__2024-05.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:21-6--case:cases/ga52_2025__2024-05.md:occ-c9efbee72fd5","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga52_2025__2024-05.html","repository_path":"cases/ga52_2025__2024-05.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":37},"excerpt":"…to the Congregation,\" but the order of service also deletes the clauses BCO 21-6 says are to be deleted for an assistant minister. The personal notes of the Presiding Minister state the vows are to be propounded to the elders.","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga52_2025__2024-05.md"},{"id":"bco:21-6--case:cases/ga52_2025__2024-05.md:occ-f7738585f8da","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga52_2025__2024-05.html","repository_path":"cases/ga52_2025__2024-05.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":37},"excerpt":"…Chairman then propounded the constitutional questions to (sic) Congregation (BCO 21.6).\" (emphasis added) The minutes continue, “The Chairman then declared that Rev. Kevin Bigelow had been regularly elected, ordained, and installed as Assistant Pastor of…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga52_2025__2024-05.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"case_numbers":["2024-5"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"TE Kevin Bigelow complained against multiple actions of North Florida Presbytery related to the dissolution of his call as Assistant Pastor of Christ Church East (where he was also serving as planting pastor at Christ Church Beaches). The SJC sustained the complaint in part (22-0-0), finding that Presbytery erred in…"}},{"id":"bco:21-6--case:cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Wilson et al. v. Pacific Northwest Presbytery","year":2023,"disposition":"dismissed","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:21-6--case:cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md:occ-29da4d4266cb","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.html","repository_path":"cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":559},"excerpt":"…after the qualifications for voters (and again in 1879 BCO 6:4:5; compare PCA BCO 21-6), the church vow to her minister read:","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md"},{"id":"bco:21-6--case:cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md:occ-1c784799650f","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.html","repository_path":"cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":617},"excerpt":"Minor communicants are not expected to provide for the “worldly maintenance\" of their minister (BCO 21-6).","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga50_2023__2022-20.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["congregational meeting","minor communicant suffrage","voting rights","communing members","church bylaws","BCO 43-1 justiciability","associate pastor resignation","Covenant Presbyterian Church","Pacific Northwest Presbytery"],"standard_of_review":"not_reached","case_numbers":["2022-20"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Members challenged a voting restriction imposed at a congregational meeting. The SJC dismissed the complaint as judicially out of order because BCO 43-1 permits complaints against acts or decisions of church courts, and a congregation is not such a court. It identified other possible routes through a report to Presbytery or review of church records. The adopted decision did not decide whether the voting restriction was constitutionally valid."}},{"id":"bco:21-6--case:cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"David Kniseley et al. v. Rocky Mountain Presbytery","year":2009,"disposition":"denied","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:21-6--case:cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md:occ-a63fa486833b","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.html","repository_path":"cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":239},"excerpt":"the questions in these two sections. BCO 21-6, 10: The","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["minister title","non-ordained staff","women","constitutional interpretation","presbytery judgment"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["2007-13"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"On complaint from TE David Kniseley and others, the SJC reviewed Rocky Mountain Presbytery's refusal to forbid a mission church from giving an unordained female staff member the title 'Minister of Church Life.' The SJC denied the complaint. It held the BCO uses 'minister' synonymously with pastor and teaching elder, but is silent on general use for non-ordained staff; a lower court may exercise discretion subject to BCO 40-2(3)'s WESP review. The decision addressed only the constitutional issue, not the title's wisdom or propriety; four commissioners dissented."}},{"id":"bco:21-6--case:cases/ga33_2005__2004-03.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga33_2005__2004-03.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Tim J. Harris v. Heritage Presbytery","year":2005,"disposition":"","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga33_2005__2004-03.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga33_2005__2004-03.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:21-6--case:cases/ga33_2005__2004-03.md:occ-5c15a5056f52","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga33_2005__2004-03.html","repository_path":"cases/ga33_2005__2004-03.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":138},"excerpt":"…in affirming the fourth vow at the time of ordination or installation (BCO 21-6.4) the congregation obliges itself to provide the pastor \"that competent worldly maintenance which you have promised and to furnish him with whatever you may see useful…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga33_2005__2004-03.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["2004-3"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"A church member challenged Heritage Presbytery's ruling that the BCO neither expressly nor implicitly requires a congregation to approve changes in a pastor's call, and that it does not require the session to publicize budget details. The SJC held the BCO silent on both points: once the original call and terms are approved, later changes are budgetary and belong to the session under BCO 12-5b; publicizing the budget is prudent but not mandated. The complaint was not sustained; seven commissioners dissented, arguing congregational approval follows by good and necessary consequence."}},{"id":"bco:21-6--case:cases/ga17_1989__case3.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga17_1989__case3.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"TE John T. DeBardeleben v. Philadelphia Presbytery","year":1989,"disposition":"sustained","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga17_1989__case3.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga17_1989__case3.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:21-6--case:cases/ga17_1989__case3.md:occ-65220540b8f6","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga17_1989__case3.html","repository_path":"cases/ga17_1989__case3.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":487},"excerpt":"…to the vows taken to provide him with a \"competent worldly maintenance\" (BCO 21-6).","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga17_1989__case3.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["complaint","trials de novo","plea bargaining","necessary witnesses","church discipline"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["1988-6"],"body":"CJB","synopsis":"A complaint challenged Philadelphia Presbytery’s approval of proceedings that cleared teaching and ruling elders without properly trying serious public accusations arising from Christ Church’s division. All three specifications were sustained because plea bargaining, dropped charges, and failure to hear necessary witnesses left the accusations unresolved. Presbytery’s action was annulled and de novo trials produced mixed convictions and acquittals. Harold Burkhart received six months’ suspension, Douglas McCready an admonition, and six former ruling elders three-month suspensions. The decision stressed taking such conflicts to Presbytery or judicial process rather than the congregation."}},{"id":"bco:21-6--overture:ga33_2005:7","record_id":"overture:ga33_2005:7","type":"Overture","title":"Amend BCO 21-5, 6, 7, 8, 10 and 22-4 Regarding Assistant Pastors","year":2005,"disposition":"Answered in the negative","authority_weight":"low-but-important","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/markdown/ga33_2005.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/markdown/ga33_2005.md","evidence_basis":"overture_action_target","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:21-6--overture:ga33_2005:7:occ-e17241900038","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/markdown/ga33_2005.html#ga33-p197","repository_path":"markdown/ga33_2005.md#ga33-p197","locator":{"fragment":"ga33-p197","page":197},"excerpt":"","sources":["disposition_bco"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/markdown/ga33_2005.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"source":"OVERTURE 7 from Chesapeake Presbytery"}},{"id":"bco:21-6--rpr_exception:rpr/exc/chesapeake__024.html","record_id":"rpr_exception:rpr/exc/chesapeake__024.html","type":"RPR exception","title":"Chesapeake: ( BCO 21-5; BCO 15; BCO 21-6; BCO 21-9) — Two installation commission reports are attached","year":2025,"disposition":"raised","authority_weight":"low-but-important","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/rpr/exc/chesapeake__024.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/rpr/exc/chesapeake__024.html","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:21-6--rpr_exception:rpr/exc/chesapeake__024.html:occ-7c73065a14df","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/rpr/exc/chesapeake__024.html","repository_path":"rpr/exc/chesapeake__024.html","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["index/rpr_search.json:provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/r